    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0419" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg369"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Mac Veagh.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-05-10"><hi rendition="#italic">May 10,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your No. 22 of the 25th
                    ultimo reporting the favorable impression made in Italy by the publication of a
                    press telegram from Washington to the effect that the U. S. Government proposed
                    taking action looking to the protection of Italian Immigrants from the padrone
                    system.</p>
                <p>For your information I inclose herewith copies of a correspondence<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d365-f1"/> which has taken place between this and the Treasury
                    Department and the Italian ambassador here on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
